Guard callback links that target loopback: in a remote workspace, a link whose
callback/redirect parameter points at localhost completes on the wrong machine
- the browser is not the host that owns the port. Which links those are is
loopbackCallback.ts in the overlay, where the spellings it has to recognise
(every name the parameter travels under, hash-queries, IPv4-mapped IPv6, up to
two levels of nesting) can be run by a test instead of read off a diff. One
concern, two halves:

- trustedDomainsValidator: warn before opening, offering Copy as the way to
  carry the link to the right machine. The check runs before the trusted-
  workspace bypass: workspace trust says nothing about where a redirect lands.
- markdown preview: absolute http(s) links otherwise navigate inside the
  preview webview and bypass the workbench opener entirely; route them through
  the existing openLink message so the guard above sees them (and tolerate
  resolveDocumentLink returning undefined for links it cannot resolve).

